# Distibution list.
# One entry per line
# Syntax: <wday> <destDir> <contact>
# where <wday>    is the day(s) of the week to distribute
#       <destDir> is the destination directory to put the distribution
#       <contact> is the user name to notify with the results
#
# Days are specified as numbers in the 0 to 6 range, Sunday to Saturday.
# A '*' indicates every day
# A comma can be used to specify selected days. e.g. 0,1,4 is Sun,Mon,&Wed.
# A range of days can be indicated with a '-'. e.g. 1-3 is same as 1,2,3
#
# The destDir is where the ExplicitDLL, ImplicitDLL, Static, and Include directories will go.
# NOTE: The destDir MUST be a UNC filename in order to work properly. So use \\nt\dev\<your path> instead of
# r:\<your path>.
#
# The contact is the email name of someone to receive the results of the
# distribution. '@digitalanvil.com' is appended to <contact> to create
# the destination email address
#
# NOTE: This distribution list is used after the daily build, which occurs in around 2:00AM each morning. Therefore,
# if you want the latest build for your use during the day on Monday, get it on Monday, not Sunday.
#

# Examples.
# This will copy the distribution built Sunday, Monday, Tuesday and Wednesday
# into the TestDir of my transfer directory, then mail me the results.
# The current testdir, if any, is renamed testdir.1.
#0,1-3 \\nt\dev\transfer\tbratton\testdir tbratton

# This will copy the distribution every day.
#* \\nt\dev\transfer\tbratton\testdir tbratton

1 \\nt\dev\projects\lancer\currentlibs jcrow

